    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d122">

                <pb facs="0280" n="262" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p1/pg262"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">790.5/1–252</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of Defense</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lovett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1952-01-02">January 2,
                        1952</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Reference is made to
                    Department of State draft negotiating paper TCT
                    D–5/9a, dated 20 December 1951, entitled “A Pacific Security Pact”.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d122-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>The Joint Chiefs of Staff have studied this matter and oppose the statement of
                    United States position as set forth in this paper, which <pb facs="0281" n="263"
                        xml:id="pg263"/> by implication indicates that the United States desires to
                    form a Pacific Area Pact similar in purpose and structure to North Atlantic
                    Treaty Organization. Their detailed comments are inclosed for your information.
                    These comments have my concurrence.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert</hi> A. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d122-a1.xml" xpointer="d122-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
